# A heap-string argument whose same-named destination receives a static output.
# The ownership flavors differ (StrH in, StrG out), so the input must keep its
# own pointer: redirecting it to the output's adapter would make this sibling
# output, which reads the input, see the adapter's value instead.
out, echo = RefineEcho(s, x)
    out = "static"
    echo = x > -1 s ⊕ "!"
